RF.put("questb:b33",{"8593":{"id":8593,"t":"Trousers of the Oracle","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Ouro's Intact Hide, 2 Idols of Life, 5 Gold Scarabs and 5 Clay Scarabs to Kandrostrasz inside Ahn'Qiraj. You must also attain Friendly reputation with the Brood of Nozdormu to complete this quest.\nOuro's Intact Hide Ouro\n2 Idol of Life Vekniss Soldier 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Stinger 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Gold Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Clay Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 3000 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","desc":"You seek to prove your worth to my kind, mortal? Very well, perhaps we can be of mutual assistance.\nThe ancient sandworm, Ouro, is a being of legendary power. He is rumored to have been created by the Old God himself as a mockery of life.\nHis skin is unnatural... thick, nearly impregnable, yet it's flexible and allows him to move with the speed and grace of a much smaller creature.\nBring me a sample of his skin along with other minor components and I shall craft you leggings of great power.","rew":"You will receive:\nTrousers of the Oracle\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"Did you bring the components I require, ‹name›?","done":"Yes... the worm's skin will make for an excellent protective layer. Combined with the strongest parts from the Qiraji we've destroyed on our way here, this should make for a formidable piece of armor. May it aid you in facing the unspeakable horrors that await inside!\nStart Kandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Kandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Both factions Class Priest Type Raid Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8593\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 16,550 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Trousers of the Oracle this quest\nBring Ouro's Intact Hide, 2 Idols of Life, 5 Gold Scarabs and 5 Clay Scarabs to Kandrostrasz inside Ahn'Qiraj.\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n9,950 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8513":{"id":8513,"t":"The Alliance Needs Medium Leather!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 1 instead of 52.","obj":"Bring 10 Medium Leather to Private Porter at the Military Ward in Ironforge.\n10 Medium Leather Tattered Chest 0 % , Battered Chest 0 % , Solid Chest 0 % , Alliance Strongbox 0 % and 4 more","desc":"Yes sir/ma'am, I have been charged with collecting and tracking all of the medium leather gathered for the war effort. If you have the wherewithal to gather medium leather, from whatever source, then please bring them to me here. I sure would appreciate a hand with this if you can spare the time.","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Alliance Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","back":"Yes sir, I remember you. Is that the medium leather you have with you there?","done":"Wow! Seems like you were just here volunteering to help. Thank you very much for the donation. I'll just get those all packed up and counted. You sure do know how to brighten a fella's day.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":60.5,"y":33.2,"n":"Private Porter","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"673":{"id":673,"t":"Foul Magics","lv":40,"min":35,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Retrieve Marez Cowl's Bloodstone Orb and bring it to Tor'gan in Hammerfall.\nBefouled Bloodstone Orb Marez Cowl","desc":"There is no doubt in my mind that a powerful warlock resides within the walls of Stromgarde. From time to time, using an arcane magical relic, this warlock has summoned forth terrible demons in large numbers. We must remove the source of his energy.\nFind the warlock and kill him. Bring me whatever magical object you find on his person, and I will take steps to destroy it and see that its power is not used to taint this land any longer.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nWhite Drakeskin Cap Radiant Silver Bracers\nExperience: 3,150\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"The burning in my blood... it grows by the day. The warlock must be stopped.","done":"My restless nights will turn to peaceful slumber when I have destroyed this orb. Thank you, ‹name›. It is a chilling reminder of the terrible power the demons held over the orcs before Hellscream released them from their curse.","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":74.7,"y":36.3,"n":"Tor'gan","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"2753":{"id":2753,"t":"Trampled Under Foot","lv":36,"min":32,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring four Green Iron Helms, four Green Iron Bracers, and two Green Iron Leggings to Orokk Omosh in Orgrimmar.\n4 Green Iron Helm\n4 Green Iron Bracers\n2 Green Iron Leggings","desc":"Only two more lessons Orokk will teach, ‹name›. Your muscles ache, I know, but continue on for the Omosh!\nBring to Orokk four green iron helms, four green iron bracers, and two green iron leggings - for this you learn and your enemies suffer!","rew":"You will receive:\nPlans: Barbaric Iron Boots\nExperience: 2,800","back":"Their skulls will crack under the pressure of your boots!","done":"You remind Orokk of his grandfather, Chief Gorokk of Omosh! Read, learn of the iron boot.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":79.2,"y":22.4,"n":"Orokk Omosh","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blacksmithing"]},"97953":{"id":97953,"t":"Camping 101 enchanting","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Vance Undergloom in Brill to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your enchanting skill to 20","desc":"Enchanters make everything better and are always welcome at any camp out in the wilds.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft an Enchanted Lute for your camp. It's so important to find entertainment during your downtime, and this bit of magic can help ensure you are ready to weather all sorts of challenges when you hit the old dusty trail once again.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Enchanted Lute. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":57.2,"y":55.4,"n":"Eleanor Shackleton","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.6,"y":51.6,"n":"Vance Undergloom","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94273":{"id":94273,"t":"Craftsmans writ moonsteel broadsword","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Moonsteel Broadsword\nMoonsteel Broadsword","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Moonsteel Broadsword, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Moonsteel Broadsword Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94273","cats":["crafting"]},"94353":{"id":94353,"t":"Craftsmans writ runecloth bag","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Runecloth Bag\nRunecloth Bag","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Runecloth Bag, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Runecloth Bag Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94353","cats":["crafting"]},"5713":{"id":5713,"t":"One Shot. One Kill.","lv":15,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Protect Sentinel Aynasha, then speak with Onaeya at Maestra's Post in Ashenvale.","desc":"I was traveling to Auberdine with an important message when I was attacked by the furbolg Marosh and his trackers. During the attack I was poisoned, leaving me barely able to stand. I can make an antidote, but it will take time before it is ready.\nI would ask that you defend me until I can apply the antidote. I will aid you with my bow as best I can.\nShould we survive, I will be able deliver my message to Auberdine, while you speak with Onaeya at Maestra's Post to inform her of this incident.","rew":"Money: 14 0 gold, 14 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,050\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Have you seen of Sentinel Aynasha on the road? She left on an important mission but she has not yet returned.","done":"You bring most welcome news ‹class›. It is good to hear that Aynasha is alive and well thanks to you. I would hope that you might accept a reward for your valor. May Elune watch over you and light your path.\nDarkshore Ashenvale","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":45.9,"y":90.3,"n":"Sentinel Aynasha","s":1},{"z":"Ashenvale","x":26.6,"y":36.7,"n":"Sentinel Onaeya","e":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"993":{"id":993,"t":"A Lost Master","lv":20,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Volcor in Darkshore and give him the Enchanted Moonstalker Cloak.\nEnchanted Moonstalker Cloak\nProvided: Enchanted Moonstalker Cloak","desc":"The cloak is complete, ‹name›. The time has come to find Volcor. I can only hope we are in time.\nThe cloak's magic, once invoked, will not last long; perhaps five minutes. It will be up to you to know when to use it: I would suggest waiting until you find Grimclaw.\nIf what he has told me is true, you will find his master in a cave south of here. Grimclaw will be alongside the road waiting for you. Signal to him by waving when you see him, and he'll point the way towards his master.","rew":"Experience: 775\n+50 reputation with Darnassus","done":"Wonderful! Terenthis found someone to help me.\nAnd look. a moonstalker cloak...<cough> Oh... that hurts. Thank you, ‹name›.\nThe furbolgs wounded me before I managed to evade them. Give me a moment, and I should be fine to talk some more.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":39.4,"y":43.5,"n":"Terenthis","s":1},{"z":"Darkshore","x":45,"y":85.3,"n":"Volcor","e":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"98913":{"id":98913,"t":"Theramore basic care package","lv":39,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Theramore Expeditionary Force","rew":"You will receive:\nTheramore Basic Care Package\nExperience: 300\n+10 reputation with The League of Arathor\nLevel 39 , requires level 30 Difficulty 30 35 37 42 49 Side Both factions Quest ID 98913","cats":["darkspear-islands"]},"94913":{"id":94913,"t":"Moonglade","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Use the spell \"Teleport: Moonglade\" to travel to Moonglade. When you arrive, speak with Dendrite Starblaze in the village of Nighthaven.","desc":"All druids are welcomed to the sacred lands of Moonglade. Keeper Remulos - Moonglade's guardian - keeps watch over all druids who hibernate there. I'll teach you the spell that lets you transport yourself there. Cast it whenever you seek Moonglade's knowledge or solace.\nAs for your first lesson here on Azeroth, travel to Moonglade and speak with Dendrite Starblaze in Nighthaven about the path you're now on. Good luck, young druid.","done":"Ah I see that you have already mastered the form of the Bear. Good, good. You are well on your way, young ‹class›.\nThunder Bluff Moonglade","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":76.4,"y":27.6,"n":"Turak Runetotem","s":1},{"z":"Moonglade","x":56.2,"y":30.4,"n":"Dendrite Starblaze","e":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"433":{"id":433,"t":"The Public Servant","lv":11,"min":6,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 10 Rockjaw Bonesnappers for Senator Mehr Stonehallow at the Gol'Bolar quarry.\nRockjaw Bonesnapper slain : 0/ 10","desc":"As a member of the Senate and the Explorers' League, I've taken it upon myself to take care of this part of the trogg infestation that has gripped our lands.\nThey've certainly made a mess of Gol'Bolar quarry, and for no reason. As we dug deep into the earth, they poured out, destroying our equipment and driving the miners out. There's not much for us to do but to exterminate the lot of them, rebuild, then get back to work.\nIf you help me with the troggs, I'll gladly recompense you for your time.","rew":"Money: 3 0 gold, 3 silver, 0 copper Experience: 650\n+75 reputation with Ironforge\n+75 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"If we can remove the troggs from Gol'Bolar quarry, it will be the first step of many that we will have to undertake to rid ourselves of this menace.","done":"It is a start. Hopefully we can take advantage of it, and move some Mountaineers in to secure the area. Then we can begin to restore our infrastructure and get the miners back to work.\nThank you for your assistance, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":68.7,"y":56,"n":"Senator Mehr Stonehallow","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"5153":{"id":5153,"t":"A Strange Historian","lv":56,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Joseph's Wedding Ring to Chromie.\nJoseph's Wedding Ring Joseph Redpath's Monument","desc":"I wish Joseph could again be with his daughter, but it cannot be so. His soul was twisted by the Scourge, and he became a monster. Oh, he is doomed!\nBut perhaps we can change his fate.\nSearch the graves outside for Joseph's monument. His body's not there, for it was trampled and destroyed years ago, but under the monument is his wedding ring. Take that ring to Chromie... a strange gnome with very strange powers.\nChromie is staying in the ruined inn at the northwest corner of Andorhal.","rew":"Experience: 4,350","back":"There is something timely about your visit. You're not from the future, are you?","done":"What is this? A wedding ring? Let me see...\nAh! This ring was once on the hand of a great man, but there is much tragedy in that man's past.\nAre you here to help him? It's far too late for him now... but perhaps we can help him in the past!","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":49.2,"y":78.6,"n":"Marlene Redpath","s":1},{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":39.5,"y":66.8,"n":"Chromie","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"33":{"id":33,"t":"Wolves Across the Border","lv":2,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 8 pieces of Tough Wolf Meat to Eagan Peltskinner outside Northshire Abbey.\n8 Tough Wolf Meat Ragged Young Wolf 80 % , Ragged Timber Wolf 80 % , Young Wolf 80 % , Timber Wolf 80 %","desc":"I hate those nasty timber wolves! But I sure like eating wolf steaks... Bring me tough wolf meat and I will exchange it for something you'll find useful.\nTough wolf meat is gathered from hunting the timber wolves and young wolves wandering the Northshire countryside.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSoft Fur-lined Shoes Wolfskin Bracers\nExperience: 170\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Hey ‹name›. I'm getting hungry...did you get that tough wolf meat?","done":"You've been busy! I can't wait to cook up that wolf meat...\nI have some things here you want - take your pick!","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":48.9,"y":40.2,"n":"Eagan Peltskinner","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"3633":{"id":3633,"t":"Goblin Engineering","lv":47,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"If you wish to learn more about Goblin Engineering, take the Manual of Engineering Disciplines to Nixx Sprocketspring in Gadgetzan.\nManual of Engineering Disciplines\nProvided: Manual of Engineering Disciplines","desc":"Expert engineering yields two distinct disciplines: gnome and goblin. Clearly, goblin engineering is the choice of all brilliant engineers. Learn to master the world through the judicious use of high explosives and fantastic gear!\n‹name›, read this manual. If you want to learn about goblin engineering, then take it to Nixx Sprocketspring in Gadgetzan. Remember - membership is permanent and prevents joining the other discipline, so make sure this is what you want before finishing his task.","rew":"Experience: 420","back":"I can smell fresh recruits much like I can an excellent blasting powder - from a mile away. Have you come seeking to learn about the mastery of the explosion?","done":"Well ‹name›, you were wise to seek my tutelage! Any schlep can become an expert at the basics of engineering - the gnomes and their irradiated home of Gnomeregan are proof of that. It takes a strong mind and a steady hand (emphasis on STEADY) though to master the discipline of Goblin Engineering.\nKeep your ears perked ‹name›, and you might learn something.\nThe Barrens Tanaris","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.7,"y":36.3,"n":"Tinkerwiz","s":1},{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.5,"y":27.3,"n":"Nixx Sprocketspring","e":1}],"cats":["engineering"]},"4113":{"id":4113,"t":"Corrupted Songflower","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"2 Cenarion Plant Salve","rew":"Experience: 550","back":"You have found a sickly, corrupted version of what appears to be a songflower plant. A pungent, unhealthy odor emanates from the plant. It desperately needs some sort of attention if it is to be turned back to normal.","done":"You apply some Cenarion plant salve to the songflower. It immediately begins to shed its corrupted form, blossoming into a vibrant and healthy plant.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":55.8,"y":10.4,"n":"Corrupted Songflower","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"8193":{"id":8193,"t":"Master Angler","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Level 60 instead of 0. Requires level 1 instead of 60.","obj":"40 Speckled Tastyfish","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nArcanite Fishing Pole Hook of the Master Angler\nMoney: 1 80 1 gold, 80 silver, 0 copper","back":"Today between 2pm and 4pm we have a contest to determine who the greatest angler of them all is! Just be the FIRST PERSON to bring me 40 Tastyfish fished from the Tastyfish schools found along the coast of Stranglethorn before anyone else does and you will be declared the Master Angler!\nIf you are not the first person to bring me 40 fish, my apprentice here will still reward you with money for each 5 Tastyfish you bring her.\nOh, and don't delay, Tastyfish go bad quickly!","done":"Hurry up and turn those in if you want to be declared the Master Angler! I have been standing around here for HOURS with nothing to eat! Hand those suckers over!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27.4,"y":76.8,"n":"Riggle Bassbait","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["fishing"]},"513":{"id":513,"t":"Elixir of Agony","lv":28,"min":24,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Mudsnout Composite to Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity.\nMudsnout Composite\nProvided: Mudsnout Composite","desc":"Just when I thought another day was going to pass devoid of any joy, you brought me those marvelous Mudsnout Blossoms.\nFirst I will mix them down into a fine composite. We'll then need Master Apothecary Faranell in the Undercity to apply his colloid of decay to it and then we'll be ready for some good fun indeed!\nHere, take this Mudsnout Composite and run it off to Master Faranell at once, ‹name›.","rew":"Experience: 1,150\n+50 reputation with Undercity","back":"Can you not see I am busy, ‹class›? The Dark Lady insists on a new plague before the Scourge advance from Northrend overwhelms us. And with the human threat pressing from the south, time becomes my most precious commodity. This better be important!","done":"Apothecary Lydon sent you? Ah, why didn't you say so!\nDespite his gloomy disposition, Apothecary Lydon is one of our most dedicated and skilled members.\nThe good chap sends Mudsnout Composite! I know what our friend in Hillsbrad is up to now. And I like the way he thinks. The Dark Lady would be most impressed with the progress he is making toward the new plague.\nHillsbrad Foothills Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":61.4,"y":19.1,"n":"Apothecary Lydon","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":48.8,"y":69.3,"n":"Master Apothecary Faranell","e":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"7633":{"id":7633,"t":"An Introduction","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","done":"Your diligence and integrity has been noted, ‹class›.\nWe are Ancients: Protectors of this once great forest. Our physical forms were destroyed 10,000 years ago when Archimonde and the Burning Legion marched upon Hyjal. Our spirits, however, remain intact.\nThere are tasks that we can offer. Tasks that if completed will open up the secrets of the Ancients to you.\nKnow this, should you complete these tasks, merely return to this rock and we shall answer the calling.\nStart Vartrus the Ancient End Vartrus the Ancient Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Class Hunter Shareable No Quest ID 7633","cats":["hunter"]},"9153":{"id":9153,"t":"Under the Shadow","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 50 instead of 58.","obj":"Check your map to find an area under Scourge attack. Go there and damage a necropolis by defeating the Scourge around them. Return 10 of their Necrotic Runes to Commander Thomas Helleran at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\n10 Necrotic Rune Bone Witch , Spirit of the Damned , Lumbering Horror , Shadow of Doom 38.4 % and 4 more","desc":"The floating necropolises of the Scourge plague the lands of Horde and Alliance alike. Tanaris, the Blasted Lands, Winterspring and the Burning Steppes are blanketed in the shadows of the flying fortresses.\nOnly through our combined efforts will they be turned away.\nThe necropolises are supported by magical circles at various points in the invaded areas. We have determined that destroying the mindless hordes that surround these circles will destroy their defenses.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\n2 Blessed Wizard Oil 2 Consecrated Sharpening Stone\n+50 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"It will take time to prevail against this threat. How have you fared, ‹name›?","done":"You've done well, ‹name›. Through these incremental defeats, we shall prevail against this renewed Scourge threat.\nRest and recover, but then you must head out to the front again, lest we lose the ground we have gained today.\nTo aid you in your further battles, we will make some of our special items available to you in trade for more necrotic runes.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.2,"y":50.6,"n":"Commander Thomas Helleran","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["invasion"]},"4513":{"id":4513,"t":"A Little Slime Goes a Long Way","lv":54,"min":48,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Filled Pure Sample Jars to Laris Geardawdle in Ironforge.\nIf you have trouble finding them, perhaps try to get more clues from Laris.\n10 Filled Pure Sample Jar\nProvided: Bag of Empty Ooze Containers","desc":"I'm going to need more samples, ‹name›. But--and I don't know how to put this--they have to be pure samples. I know, I know. \"What does 'pure' mean, Laris?\" I'm not sure. I do know that these are corrupt... just like Felwood. Which is what makes my realization so important. The oozes seem to adapt... to take on the aspects of the area they're in. I'll need to find samples that haven't been polluted. But where? Where?!\nBah! ‹name›, take these containers just in case you find any on your own.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nHazecover Boots Brazen Gauntlets\nMoney: 40 0 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,800\n+150 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"So many things to consider. But what does it mean? And how does it affect the lives of the people of Azeroth?","done":"You've found it? ‹name›, you are a treasure unto yourself. Your dedication and aid has been magnificent and I could not possibly thank you enough.\nPlease, take this for your troubles. I have some work to do, but I'm sure, if you come back at a later time, I'll have need of your services again.\nThank you. Thank you so much.\nDun Morogh Un'Goro Crater","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":63.2,"y":24.8,"n":"Laris Geardawdle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"273":{"id":273,"t":"Resupplying the Excavation","lv":15,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Huldar.","desc":"It's not too late though, you're welcome to go look for Huldar. He can't have made it very far, strong as they are, Miran and Saean can only move so fast laden down with those barrels.\nThey're taking the normal route to the site, leaving south out of town and following the curve of the Loch.\nShouldn't have a problem finding them unless they've already gotten there.","rew":"Experience: 270\n+25 reputation with Ironforge","done":"Hmph, it'll take more than a Dark Iron ambush to stop the deliveries!\nBut Saean... I would never have suspected him to be one of their sympathizers. We've been working with him for almost a year now... maybe I missed the signs.\nWell, I'll consider that later.","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":37.2,"y":47.4,"n":"Jern Hornhelm","s":1},{"z":"Loch Modan","x":52.2,"y":69.3,"n":"Huldar","e":1}],"cats":["loch-modan"]},"8673":{"id":8673,"t":"Bloodhoof the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"Your spirit burns with life, young ‹class›. I accept the homage you pay, and offer in return this token...","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":47.5,"y":57.8,"n":"Elder Bloodhoof","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"1953":{"id":1953,"t":"Return to the Marsh","lv":40,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Tabetha.","desc":"It is time, ‹name›, for you to speak with Tabetha... the hermit of Dustwallow Marsh. She will instruct you on the creation of a powerful mage's implement.\nTabetha's shack lies deep in Dustwallow Marsh, west of Theramore.","rew":"Experience: 320","done":"Ah, yes. You are here for an orb or a staff, ‹name›? Very well. I will aid you in its construction.\nBut be forewarned--the process is a perilous one and could mean your death.\nOr my death. Definitely someone's death...\nBut let's hope it's someone else's death, eh?\nUndercity Dun Morogh Stormwind City Orgrimmar Dustwallow Marsh","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":85.1,"y":10,"n":"Anastasia Hartwell","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":55.5,"y":22.4,"n":"Bink","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":49.6,"y":85.8,"n":"Jennea Cannon","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":39.2,"y":86.3,"n":"Uthel'nay","s":1},{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":46.1,"y":57.1,"n":"Tabetha","e":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"753":{"id":753,"t":"A Humble Task","lv":3,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take a Water Pitcher from the water well.\nReturn the pitcher to Chief Hawkwind in Camp Narache which is northwest from the water well.\nWater Pitcher Water Pitcher , Water Pitcher","desc":"I have traveled many paths through life and these old legs lack the vigor they once had. I can still perform my duties to the tribe. Sometimes it just takes an old woman a little longer to do the task.\nBut you look like an eager ‹class›. Let's put some of that youthful vitality to the test. Take a water pitcher from the well and bring it to my son, the Chief, in Camp Narache.\nRemember that even the most humble task can gain the recognition of elders.","rew":"Money: 40 0 gold, 0 silver, 40 copper Experience: 250\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"You look as though you have returned from the plains. Do you have any word from Greatmother Hawkwind?","done":"You carried this pitcher back at the Greatmother's bidding, I see.\nYour willingness to help others and provide for the tauren of Camp Narache leads me to believe you would make the tribe proud in Thunder Bluff someday.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":48.8,"y":80.9,"n":"Greatmother Hawkwind","s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":43.9,"y":76.7,"n":"Chief Hawkwind","e":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"833":{"id":833,"t":"A Sacred Burial","lv":10,"min":7,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Lorekeeper Raintotem wants you to kill 8 Bristleback Interlopers at Red Rocks.\nBristleback Interloper slain : 0/ 8","desc":"Only the most valiant tauren are laid to rest at Red Rocks, our sacred burial ground. It is an honor bestowed upon the great warriors who helped found and defend Thunder Bluff and those who have given their lives for the greater good of their tribes and chieftains.\nBut it appears a foul menace has made its way onto our holy land. A band of Bristleback Interlopers is ravaging the grave site and I am too old and past my prime to drive them away.\nThey must be driven off with force, ‹name›.","rew":"Money: 2 50 0 gold, 2 silver, 50 copper Experience: 625\n+75 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"The Bristleback Interlopers must be driven away from our sacred burial ground, ‹name›.","done":"Well done. You have sent those foul Bristlebacks a clear message. They will think twice before attempting to meddle in this holy spot again.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":57,"y":34.5,"n":"Lorekeeper Raintotem","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"9073":{"id":9073,"t":"Earthshatter Handguards","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Rimblat Earthshatter at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Earthshatter Handguards if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Handguards, 8 Wartorn Chain Scraps, 1 Arcanite Bar and 5 Cured Rugged Hides.\nDesecrated Handguards\n8 Wartorn Chain Scrap Stoneskin Gargoyle 14.4 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 13.5 % in Naxxramas , Spirit of Naxxramas 13.3 % in Naxxramas , Living Monstrosity 12.5 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\nArcanite Bar\n5 Cured Rugged Hide","desc":"Would you honor me by returning the armor of those that fell in the defense of these lands?\nThe armor has been desecrated and is undoubtedly being used for evil; however, with wartorn armor scraps, the desecrated armor can be renewed and worn for battle once more.\nBring me the remnants of the fallen along with purification materials and Earthshatter shall be yours to don.\nSearch Naxxramas.","rew":"You will receive:\nEarthshatter Handguards\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Have you brought me that which I require?","done":"These handguards channel the power of the elements!","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.3,"y":49.4,"n":"Rimblat Earthshatter","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"9233":{"id":9233,"t":"Omarion's Handbook","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take Omarion's Handbook to Craftsman Wilhelm at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nOmarion's Handbook\nProvided: Omarion's Handbook","desc":"Wilhelm,\nIf you are reading this, I have perished - finally. I want you to know that my dying thoughts revolved around you and your ineptitude when it comes to tradeskills. Unfortunately, the bearer of this handbook is in even worse shape than you in regards to crafting.\nAbout the book: These are the rest of my recipes. Make the bearer of this book whatever they request. I'm sure you will charge a hefty fee for your services because you are, after all, a bastard.\nIn Disdain,\nOmarion","back":"Is that what I think it is?\n<Wilhelm appears to be drooling.>","done":"He musta really been off his rocker when he wrote this! Omarion and I - we were thick as thieves!\nAnyhow, this certainly opens up some new possibilities, ‹name›. I am now able to craft more items - for a small fee and material charges, of course.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.2,"y":49.9,"n":"Craftsman Wilhelm","e":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"8913":{"id":8913,"t":"An Earnest Proposition","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -20g instead of 0.","obj":"Acquire 15 Silithus Venom Samples and 20 gold and bring them along with a set of Wildheart Bracers to Mokvar in Orgrimmar.\n15 Silithus Venom Sample Stonelash Scorpid 30 % , Stonelash Pincer 30 % , Stonelash Flayer 30 % , Sand Skitterer 30 % and 1 more\nWildheart Bracers Wailing Banshee 4.6 % in Stratholme , Crimson Inquisitor 4.5 % , Shrieking Banshee 3.9 % in Stratholme , Diseased Ghoul 1.4 % in Scholomance","desc":"Hail, ‹class›! I can tell by your demeanor that you've seen and done much in this world. Yet I'm willing to wager you haven't seen a piece of armor like this.\nPerform a small favor for me and I'll be willing to trade it to you for an ordinary set of bracers.\nI'm in need of a sizeable sample of venom drawn from the spiders and scorpions that inhabit Silithus. Bring this to me along with a few gold coins and I'll perform the exchange.","rew":"You will receive:\nFeralheart Bracers\nExperience: 6,600","back":"Have you obtained the items I require, ‹name›?","done":"Ah, yes. Mux will be quite happy with this.\nThose bracers were part of a larger armor set. If you're interested in providing me with further assistance, I'd be willing to consider parting with the rest of it.\nOrgrimmar Silithus","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":34.9,"y":38.3,"n":"Mokvar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"1793":{"id":1793,"t":"The Tome of Valor","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nTome of Valor","done":"It has been proven that the Light is with you, ‹name›, but as times grow more dangerous, it becomes important to know what strength lies beneath the flesh. When demons, dragons, or any other evil set foot in your lands, your mettle will be tested. Will you be strong enough?\nBravery, regardless of the situation, is as much a part of paladinhood as the Light, your armor, and your weapon. Protecting the weak, and not losing faith are two more lessons you must master while you study in the Cathedral of Light.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":50.5,"y":47.5,"n":"Duthorian Rall","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"5633":{"id":5633,"t":"Returning Home","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Priestess Alathea in Darnassus.","desc":"Greetings, laddy/lass. Good to see you here in our great halls. A blessing be on you and your kind.\nWhile you were traveling through our lands, a priestess of your temple came here seeking you. She said that you were to return to the Temple of the Moon as soon as possible. I'm sorry I can't tell you more, but it did sound important. When you get to the temple, speak to a Priestess Alathea.","rew":"You will learn: Starshards\nExperience: 210","done":"Wonderful, you've returned home, ‹name›. It always pleases Tyrande and myself when those we've trained go out into the world and return to us safely. How have things been with you? Does Elune still bless your travels? Perhaps after we speak more about the business at hand, you could tell me more of your travels.\nDun Morogh Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":55,"y":22.6,"n":"Braenna Flintcrag","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":39.5,"y":81.2,"n":"Priestess Alathea","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"8833":{"id":8833,"t":"Ten Commendation Signets","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"10 Horde Commendation Signet","back":"I accept commendation signets from adventurers who have received them in the line of duty. For each set of ten that you hand to me, I'll make sure that you receive a significant acknowledgement of your deeds with Undercity. I also accept single tokens, but at a much reduced rate of recognition. We are much more interested in greater feats of duty, though no feat will be ignored.\nWith that said, I'll gladly take your signets if you are ready to hand in a set.","done":"Excellent! It is no small sacrifice that you've made to earn these signets, and you will be acknowledged for your service appropriately. It's adventurers like you, ‹name›, that truly make a difference.\nLet me know if you have additional signets to hand in; I'll gladly help you out with whatever ones you need exchanged.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":42.5,"y":38.7,"n":"Officer Redblade","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["reputation"]},"8353":{"id":8353,"t":"Chicken Clucking for a Mint","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Do a chicken emote at Innkeeper Firebrew, and in exchange you'll receive an Ironforge Mint!","desc":"Ah, trick-or-treating for a sick child, are we? I was going to say, you're a little old to be rummaging about for candies...\nWell, for my treat - an Ironforge Mint - you will need to... cluck like a chicken! Yes, chickens love mints... well OK, maybe they don't LOVE them... but I won't give you a mint unless you chicken cluck for me!\nWell ‹class›, are you up to the challenge or not?! Time to earn your treat!","rew":"You will receive:\nIronforge Mint","done":"Too funny! Well done, ‹name›! Here's your treat.\nHappy Hallow's End!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":54,"y":29.3,"n":"Innkeeper Firebrew","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"8993":{"id":8993,"t":"Gift Giving","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Alliance Gift Collection","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\n5 Handful of Rose Petals 5 Silver Shafted Arrow\nYou will also receive:\nBox of Chocolates","back":"Have you come to deliver a present of love and adoration to your favorite leader?","done":"Wonderful! Wonderful! I will add this to the pile of other gifts.\nI didn't expect so many! You must truly love your leaders.\nNow, let me just add one more to the count...\nUndercity Darnassus Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":55.2,"y":89.9,"n":"Kwee Q. Peddlefeet","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":38.1,"y":80.5,"n":"Kwee Q. Peddlefeet","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":57.5,"y":30.2,"n":"Kwee Q. Peddlefeet","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"81953":{"id":81953,"t":"Stonewrought design","lv":45,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Stonewrought Design","rew":"You will receive:\nItem 211779\nMoney: 6 0 gold, 6 silver, 0 copper Experience: 390","back":"Have you brought something to add to our collection?\nStonewrought Design (1)","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Our knowledge expands through your efforts.\nIf you discover more magical works that might benefit the library, please bring them to me.\nStormwind City Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":37.8,"y":80.2,"n":"Garion Wendell","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":73.6,"y":33,"n":"Owen Thadd","e":1}],"cats":["special"]},"1073":{"id":1073,"t":"Ineptitude + Chemicals = Fun","lv":21,"min":17,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 4 Minor Mana Potions and 2 Elixirs of Minor Fortitude to Lomac Gearstrip in Ironforge.\n4 Minor Mana Potion Qiraji Officer Zod 80 % , Qiraji Officer 80 % , Eroded Anubisath Warbringer 70 % , Minor Anubisath Warbringer 35 % and 4 more\n2 Elixir of Minor Fortitude","desc":"Hahaha... you need Nitromirglyceronium to stop goblins from destroying a forest?!\nI don't care if you know Gaxim or not... I'll give you the stuff just to see you or them explode into itty bitty pieces.\nThere's a problem though: I'm all out.\nBut I'll tell you what, you bring me the correct potions, and I'll make some up for you right away.\nThe least you can do is prove you've got some skill as an alchemist before I just give you a sample of my greatest creation.","rew":"Experience: 1,650\n+100 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"I can't make any Nitromirglyceronium if I don't have the potions... they're vital to its creation.","done":"This'll do nicely.\nIf I didn't know better, stranger, I'd say you knew somethin' about alchemy. Good, good... the world's not all about swords and sorcery, you know?\nDun Morogh Loch Modan Wetlands","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.7,"y":29.4,"n":"Lomac Gearstrip","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"353":{"id":353,"t":"Stormpike's Delivery","lv":15,"min":9,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver the Package for Stormpike to Mountaineer Stormpike in Loch Modan.\nPackage for Stormpike\nProvided: Package for Stormpike","desc":"The Stormpikes are a respected dwarven clan, and are well known for their fine and discerning tastes. So it's no wonder that Gringer Stormpike, a Mountaineer of Ironforge, commissioned me to craft him a weapon.\nThe weapon is finished, but... Mountaineer Stormpike is far away, in distant Loch Modan. If you plan on traveling to the north, can you deliver this package to him?\nMy last message from Mountaineer Stormpike said he's stationed at the northern guard tower in Loch Modan.","rew":"Money: 7 0 gold, 7 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,050\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"You come all the way from Stormwind? I hear it's getting dicey down there in the human lands, with brigands and orcs running about. A perfect place for a ‹class› to prove his worth!","done":"Aha! So Grimand finally finished my axe! I can't wait to try it against some troggs and kobolds!\nMany thanks, ‹name›. It was a long distance to travel for this delivery. Here are some coins for your efforts.\nStormwind City Loch Modan","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":59.7,"y":33.8,"n":"Grimand Elmore","s":1},{"z":"Loch Modan","x":24.8,"y":18.4,"n":"Mountaineer Stormpike","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"7793":{"id":7793,"t":"A Donation of Silk","lv":60,"min":26,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"60 Silk Cloth Protector Weaver , Mountaineer Langarr 85.7 % , Watcher Wollpert 85.7 % , Mountaineer Zwarn 78.3 % and 4 more","rew":"Experience: 1,650\n+150 reputation with Stormwind","back":"As with most other fabrics, our stocks of silk are at an all-time low. Our stores are such that we'd only need sixty pieces of silk from you total; we should be able to reach our goal with the support of others.\nA benevolent gift such as silk, might I add, would certainly increase your local standing in the community! If you have the sixty pieces of silk cloth on you and are ready to donate them, I'm able to take them from you now.","done":"Wonderful! We thank you for your generous donation, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":53.9,"y":81.7,"n":"Clavicus Knavingham","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"193":{"id":193,"t":"Panther Mastery","lv":40,"min":28,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Sir S. J. Erlgadin of Nesingwary's Expedition wants you to bring him the Fang of Bhag'thera.\nFang of Bhag'thera Bhag'thera","desc":"You've almost proven yourself to be a master hunter of panthers. A panther by the name of Bhag'thera has been prowling the jungle. So far he's eluded our party. See if you can use your skills to kill the great Bhag'thera.\nBring me the Fang of Bhag'thera and you'll have earned my respect!","rew":"You will receive:\nPanther Hunter Leggings\nExperience: 3,150","back":"Bhag'thera can prove to be an elusive beast. How fares the hunt?","done":"So the great Bhag'thera is dead! Cheers to you, ‹name›. You are a mighty ‹class› indeed!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":35.6,"y":10.5,"n":"Sir S. J. Erlgadin","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"593":{"id":593,"t":"Filling the Soul Gem","lv":46,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Soul Gem","rew":"You will receive:\nFilled Soul Gem","back":"Yenniku stands stunned before you, his mind in another place...","done":"You place the Soul Gem upon his forehead. He shudders as his soul is sucked in, leaving his body, a mindless husk, behind.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":39,"y":58.3,"n":"Yenniku","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"1393":{"id":1393,"t":"Galen's Escape","lv":38,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Escort Galen out of danger, then find his camp in the Swamp of Sorrows and open his strongbox.","desc":"Please help! These creatures are going to eat me!\nHelp me out of here, and I'll give you a great treasure! It's in my camp in the swamp north of Stonard, but it's locked in a strongbox that can be opened through a trick that only I know.\nIf you help me escape, then I'll teach it to you.","rew":"You will receive:\nVisionary Buckler\nMoney: 85 0 gold, 85 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,850\n+50 reputation with Alliance\n+50 reputation with Horde","back":"The keyhole of this strongbox is filled with black resin. It is impossible to open.","done":"The keyhole of this strongbox is filled with black resin. It is impossible to open.\nBut Galen told you of a hidden latch on the box's bottom...\n...After a quick search the latch is found. The latch is flipped, and the strongbox opens...","pins":[{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":65.5,"y":18.2,"n":"Galen Goodward","s":1},{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":47.8,"y":39.8,"n":"Galen's Strongbox","e":1}],"cats":["swamp-of-sorrows"]},"113":{"id":113,"t":"Insect Part Analysis","lv":48,"min":39,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver the report to Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser in Gadgetzan. Be sure he gives you a copy of the report, as Alchemist Pestlezugg has requested.\nInsect Analysis Report\nProvided: Insect Analysis Report","desc":"Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser needs to see this report immediately. Actually... everyone who can read needs to see this report. We are facing a grave and serious threat to not only Tanaris and Gadgetzan, but if left unchecked, the entirety of southern Kalimdor. Heck, even quite possible the whole of Azeroth; this thing has given no indication it will subside.\nHave Fizzledowser make a duplicate of the report for you to distribute freely to your allegiance. Everyone must know about this threat!","rew":"Money: 70 0 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 440\n+10 reputation with Gadgetzan","back":"Well Junior Surveyor ‹name›, has ol' Pestlezugg got that report ready yet?","done":"Thank you for delivering the report, Junior Surveyor ‹name›; here is your pay for your diligent service to the Gadgetzan Water Company.\nWhile I am usually not thrilled about handing out our valuable information carte blanche to those who would otherwise pay good coin for it, I've known Pestlezugg for a number of years now. If he recommends letting everyone know about it, then so be it. Give me a moment and I'll make you a copy.","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":50.9,"y":27,"n":"Alchemist Pestlezugg","s":1},{"z":"Tanaris","x":50.2,"y":27.5,"n":"Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser","e":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"8753":{"id":8753,"t":"The Path of the Conqueror","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Signet Ring of the Bronze Dragonflight","rew":"You will receive:\nSignet Ring of the Bronze Dragonflight\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"Your continued defense of the children of Kalimdor has been acknowledged. Hand me your signet ring so that I may enhance its powers.","done":"Your rise amongst the rank of the Brood is most impressive, ‹name›. May you never stray from the path of the conqueror!","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.3,"y":50,"n":"Anachronos","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"99073":{"id":99073,"t":"Easing suffering","lv":10,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Take the Lashwater Salve to Sentinel Eralya Leafshadow on the road to the Oracle Tree.\nProvided: Lashwater Salve","desc":"The salve is ready. Take it to Eralya swiftly.\nI do not know if it will truly cure her. The rot festers quickly, and grows in strength as it spreads.\nIt will, if nothing else, ease her suffering. And that is still worth your haste.","back":"<Eralya has stopped responding verbally. Only a weak, gurgled exhale confirms life.>","done":"<Eralya's breath calms quickly as you help her ingest the salve. She may not survive, but is at relative peace.>","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":55.2,"y":56.8,"n":"Byancie","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":37.6,"y":36.8,"n":"Sentinel Eralya Leafshadow","e":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"913":{"id":913,"t":"Cry of the Thunderhawk","lv":20,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find and slay a Thunderhawk, return its wings to Jorn Skyseer at Camp Taurajo.\nThunderhawk Wings Thunderhawk Hatchling , Greater Thunderhawk , Thunderhawk Cloudscraper","desc":"The thunderhawk, ‹name›, is a fierce beast. It is time for you to face them. You must find where it roams, and bring me its wings as proof of your successful hunt.\nDo this, and your time with me will near its end.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nCobalt Buckler Wind Rider Staff\nYou will also receive:\nGloves of the Moon\nExperience: 1,950\n+150 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Is it done? Have you slain the thunderhawk?","done":"You, like the thunderhawk, should be proud. You have bested every foe we set you before, and have done so with strength, courage and honor.\nBut your path, ‹name›, continues. In fact, you will find that true hunters forever strive, forever walk their path with the same pride you have shown me.\nNow, it is time to move on.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":44.9,"y":59.1,"n":"Jorn Skyseer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"1153":{"id":1153,"t":"A New Ore Sample","lv":29,"min":25,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find an Unrefined Ore Sample on a Gravelsnout Digger or Surveyor and bring it to Tatternack Steelforge at Camp Taurajo in the Barrens.\nUnrefined Ore Sample Gravelsnout Surveyor 20 % , Gravelsnout Digger 20 % , Gibblesnik 20 %","desc":"‹class›, you have done well in helping me in the past. The warchief is pleased thus far with what I've accomplished, and asks me to continue with renewed determination. My honor dictates that I give you proper recognition to the warchief for all you have done, but first I would ask you for your help again.\nTravelers recently came from the south from a place called Thousand Needles. There they killed a kobold who had an unusual ore sample, but they would not sell it. I want a sample of that ore to examine.","rew":"You will receive:\nOrcish War Sword\nMoney: 25 0 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,350\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"I saw the travelers again - the ones that would not sell me a sample of the ore. I spit at them for not helping the warchief.\nMay they die in battle like cowards and not like warriors as should be the right of all people who ally themselves with the Horde.","done":"A good sample, ‹name›. A good sample indeed.\nThose travelers can no longer lord over me the ore they found, now that you have been successful.\nI shall get to work on it immediately. If it proves strong enough, I will send a weapon crafted from the material back to the warchief to show him our success.\nI shall not forget your help, ‹class›.\nThe Barrens Thousand Needles","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":45.1,"y":57.7,"n":"Tatternack Steelforge","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"8273":{"id":8273,"t":"Oran's Gratitude","lv":47,"min":42,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nUndercity Reservist's Cap Antiquated Nobleman's Tunic\nMoney: 70 0 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,200\n+50 reputation with Undercity","done":"Now isn't this interesting? You say you found this tablet on a small, deserted island at The Overlook Cliffs in The Hinterlands, ‹class›? Very interesting indeed. <Oran carefully puts the tablet away and rubs her hands together.>\nI thank you for your efforts in this matter. Our Dark Lady shall be very pleased with this discovery. Here, allow me to reward you proportionately.","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":73.1,"y":32.8,"n":"Oran Snakewrithe","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-hinterlands"]},"2993":{"id":2993,"t":"Return to the Hinterlands","lv":47,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Gryphon Master Talonaxe.","desc":"Sharpbeak is held in a cage, high on a cliff at the top of Jintha'Alor in the Hinterlands. The key to this cage is possessed by the high priestess of the Vilebranch trolls, Vile Priestess Hexx.\nThere. I have done my part. I bid you fortune on your quest, ‹name›.","rew":"Experience: 2,100\n+50 reputation with Wildhammer Clan","done":"You've spoken with Grimshade? What did he say?\n...What? The Vilebranch trolls have Sharpbeak? That's unbearable! We must organize a force to get him back!\nBlasted Lands The Hinterlands","pins":[{"z":"Blasted Lands","x":66.9,"y":19.5,"n":"Thadius Grimshade","s":1},{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":9.8,"y":44.5,"n":"Gryphon Master Talonaxe","e":1}],"cats":["the-hinterlands"]},"99153":{"id":99153,"t":"The one that got away","lv":10,"min":7,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find the Hidden Crystal Fragment beneath Shadowvale for Ephram Barbaro.\nGlowing Crystal Fragment","desc":"Oi, you! Word travels quickly among our ranks. I heard about the work you did with the cultists around the remnants of the battle with Naxxramas.\nProblem is, one of them cultists got away with a piece of the focusing crystal. Seems to still have some juice in it. Best guess we have is it's somewhere beneath Shadowvale. It's either raising 'em or making 'em stronger, and you don't want either one.\nFind that crystal before this gets out of hand.","back":"Did you find the damned thing?","done":"Well done--and quick, too! Now onto my favorite part...","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":20.2,"y":46.4,"n":"Ephram Barbaro","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"1473":{"id":1473,"t":"Creature of the Void","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Recover Egalin's Grimoire and bring it to Carendin Halgar in the Temple of the Damned.\nEgalin's Grimoire Perrine's Chest","desc":"It seems the consensus that you are ready to learn to summon a voidwalker.\nA being created of the chaos that lies beyond, if you summon one but cannot control it, you will be torn asunder.\nThe first voidwalker was summoned by Egalin, and in his grimoire is the process explained.\nUnfortunately, it was stolen from us by an agent of the Scarlet Crusade who has it secreted away in his base at a tower to the west. Bring it to me, and I will impart the knowledge to you.","rew":"Experience: 625","back":"Egalin was the teacher that taught me. With hardly a look, he was able to command the voidwalker he had summoned.\nWhen it came my turn to try, I was overconfident. Do not trifle with the powers that you wield, ‹name›, they can consume even the vigilant.","done":"Ah, this is excellent. Like as not, Perrine was ignorant to the true power of the musty book he had stolen from us.\nIt will not fall out of our hands again. Observe, ‹name›, the structure of the spell, the manner in which your power must be channeled.\nUndercity Tirisfal Glades","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":85.1,"y":26,"n":"Carendin Halgar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"1713":{"id":1713,"t":"The Summoning","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Whirlwind Heart to Bath'rah Windwatcher.\nWhirlwind Heart Cyclonian","desc":"I am ready to perform the ritual to summon Cyclonian. When he is summoned, you must defeat him and take his whirlwind heart. This I will use to instill a weapon with Cyclonian's power.\n‹name›, are you ready to face the wind lord?","rew":"Experience: 2,350","back":"‹name›, I must have the whirlwind heart!","done":"You did it! You defeated Cyclonian and gained the Whirlwind Heart!","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":80.5,"y":66.9,"n":"Bath'rah the Windwatcher","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"8433":{"id":8433,"t":"Battle of Warsong Gulch","lv":49,"min":40,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Warsong Marks of Honor to a Horde Warbringer outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Warsong Gulch Mark of Honor","desc":"The battle in Warsong Gulch against the Silverwing Sentinels is of great importance. Under the guise of protecting a forest that doesn't belong to them, the Alliance seeks to deny the Horde one of our largest sources for lumber.\nDo not let this happen, ‹name›! Come back to me with proof of serving the Horde in a worthy manner!","rew":"Experience: 2,250\n+50 reputation with Warsong Outriders","back":"The battle in Warsong Gulch against the Silverwing Sentinels is of great importance. Under the guise of protecting a forest that doesn't belong to them, the Alliance seeks to deny the Horde one of our largest sources for lumber.\nDo not let this happen, ‹name›! Come back to me with proof of serving the Horde in a worthy manner!","done":"Excellent! You've shown your worth by defending our operations in Warsong Gulch! May word of your honor spread far and wide across our lands.\nThe Barrens Arathi Highlands Undercity","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":46.7,"y":8.7,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.5,"y":29.1,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":58.3,"y":97.9,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warsong-gulch"]},"7873":{"id":7873,"t":"Vanquish the Invaders!","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 5,650 experience instead of 8,150, 0.69 times as much.","obj":"Enter Warsong Gulch and defeat the Horde, obtain a Warsong Gulch Mark of Honor, and return to Sentinel Farsong at the Silverwing Grove.\nWarsong Gulch Mark of Honor","desc":"Beyond this tunnel you will find a field of strife and turmoil, young ‹class›. The Horde continue to decimate our sacred forest, cutting down the evergreen foliage to power their machines of war.\nEnter Warsong Gulch and defend Silverwing Hold. Push back the invading Horde forces!\nDo this, and earn a talisman of merit. Bring me such a talisman, ‹name›, and I shall reward you.","rew":"Money: 2 50 2 gold, 50 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,650\n+200 reputation with Silverwing Sentinels\n+200 reputation with Silverwing Sentinels\n+200 reputation with Silverwing Sentinels\n+200 reputation with Silverwing Sentinels\nLevel 55 , requires level 50 Difficulty 50 51 53 58 Side Human, Dwarf, Night Elf, Gnome Type PvP Shareable No Repeatable Yes Quest ID 7873","cats":["warsong-gulch"]},"5233":{"id":5233,"t":"Target: Writhing Haunt","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Go to the Writhing Haunt in Western Plaguelands to locate and defeat the Cauldron Lord present there, and use its key to gain access to the cauldron. You must have the Empty Writhing Haunt Bottle with you to secure a sample of the poisons used inside the cauldron.\nWrithing Haunt Cauldron Key Cauldron Lord Razarch\nEmpty Writhing Haunt Bottle\nProvided: Empty Writhing Haunt Bottle","desc":"Two cauldrons have been successfully opened; while you'll be able to access them indefinitely, we still want to open up the other two that remain. This will provide all of us with more options to introduce the counter agent!\nThis time, you'll be hitting the Writhing Haunt's cauldron. It is almost due east of Andorhal, relatively close to the ruined city walls; again, eliminate the cauldron lord present there for its key. Use this bottle to obtain the sample from the cauldron.\nGood hunting, ‹name›!","rew":"Experience: 5,650\n+100 reputation with Undercity\n+100 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"An access panel to the cauldron remains securely fastened. In order to open it, you will need to find the key.","done":"The cauldron lord's key unlocks the access panel to this cauldron and then disappears, much like the other keys have for the previous ones you've dealt of. A putrid smelling substance churns violently beneath the platform of the cauldron.\nThere is a small spigot that the bottle fits well enough under, allowing you to draw a sample for Shadow Priestess Vandis back at the Bulwark.\nTirisfal Glades Western Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":83,"y":71.9,"n":"Shadow Priestess Vandis","s":1},{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":53,"y":65.6,"n":"Scourge Cauldron","e":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"92753":{"id":92753,"t":"Destruction in deadmines","lv":18,"min":9,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which halved what dungeon quests give beyond a normal quest.","obj":"Find the forge hidden in the Deadmines, and plant the Extra-Destructive Explosives nearby. Then, meet up with Alba Fairmoon at the Deadmines exit.\nExplosives placed\nProvided: Extra-Destructive Explosives","desc":"The source of the poison is likely a large metallurgical forge of some kind. Find a way into the Deadmines and locate the forge, then place the explosives.\nI will wait for you in the hills behind Moonbrook. Once you return, we can detonate the explosives. Hopefully with the forge gone, the land can begin to heal.","done":"So you found the forge, and planted the bomb... only one thing remains to be done.","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":52.4,"y":53,"n":"Alba Fairmoon","s":1},{"z":"Westfall","x":38.6,"y":83.6,"n":"Alba Fairmoon","e":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"8113":{"id":8113,"t":"Pristine Enchanted South Seas Kelp","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60.","obj":"Enchanted South Seas Kelp","rew":"You will receive:\nPristine Enchanted South Seas Kelp\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"‹name›! It been a long time since I seen you. Did you know that King Rastakhan himself be givin' me the order to add the final bit of mojo and magic to your talisman? It be true, mon! I wouldn't have believed it had I not seen it with me own eyes. Give it here.","done":"‹name› mon, it been a good journey. Keep on with the killing and suppressing of Hakkar and he minions.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":16,"n":"Maywiki of Zuldazar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zulgurub"]}});